  "aiperf_view": "AIPerf 0.13.0's own MooncakeTrace model + MooncakeTraceDatasetLoader._group_traces/convert_to_conversations on aiperf_input.jsonl (AIPerf env), projected as the timing strategies consume it (Turn.metadata timestamp_ms/delay_ms; FixedScheduleStrategy stable sort and auto offset; raw_payload as sent).",
  "replay_reference": "written in audit_parity.py from the replay source, not from the generator: aisimulate-core 0.13.0-dev.202609300000000061 replay/loadgen/trace.rs MooncakeTraceBuilder::push (session keys, ISL default, delay/delay_ms/timestamp-difference), normalize_session_starts + speed_up_timing (trace.rs:892-923), HashIdInterner + synthesize_validated_trace_tokens (trace.rs:255-358); Dynamo lib/mocker/src/replay/entrypoints.rs:131-152 (all-single-turn open loop -> no SessionContext) and offline/entrypoints.rs:562-593 (closed loop -> SessionContext always).",
  "replay_rows": "cached lr-eval per_request rows (CR/runs/cache/results, build 6955b0ee, matching cell content SHA and replicate trace SHA) for 2 policies per cell; arrivals of later turns and closed-loop starts are policy-dependent, so every check runs per policy.",
  "stub_runtime": "AIPerf 0.13.0 run with the manifest's exact argv/env (run_aiperf.py) against audit_stub_server.py, which identifies each request by prompt digest and answers with replay's own TTFT/E2E for it; four full cells (45,462 requests). The AIPerf export is then scored with score_live (cell measure, AIS E0) and compared with replay's record.",
  "prefix_pairs": "per cell 750 pairs in each stratum: same first hash block, same first 3 blocks, same session (multi-turn cells), uniform",
  "block_structure": "blake2b-8 chained hash of every full 16-token block of every AIPerf prompt vs the same hash over replay's synthesized tokens; a bijection means the KV router and the vLLM prefix cache see the same reuse structure"
 },
